President Trump will meet with Russian  President Vladimir Putin and Chinese  President Xi Jinping at the g20 summit  in Japan next month now this meeting  comes amid an escalation of what author  Jim Sciuto calls a new type of warfare  his new book it's called the shadow war  inside Russia's and China's secret  operations to defeat America and it's on  big time it highlights tactics he says  both countries use to attack the US and  its allies but fall below the thrust the  threshold of starting a shooting war try  saying that three times  shuto is CNN's chief national security  correspondent and anchor he's also  served as chief of staff to America's  ambassador to China from 2011 to 2013  and we're delighted that you were at the  table mr. great severe thanks so much  for having me so we all have heard the  term cold war trade war but this shadow  war is a different kind of animal you  say and they use very different tactics  like it is it's a war that they are  waging Russia and China are waging on  the US and we're not fighting back and  only very recently came to terms with it  and I think Americans are aware of or  some of the fronts of this war certainly  election interference which continues  but but they're not aware of others  Russia and China have both put weapons  in space lasers kamikaze satellites  kidnapper satellites a China has  developed a satellite that could grab  other satellites out of orbit these are  satellites we depend on for the way we  live every day of our lives GPS etc but  also the military does crucially there  is a new great game under the waves  submarine warfare between the US Russia  and China submarines they're quieter  they're getting closer to us Shores  that's a way to project nuclear power  without warning right up to the US  homeland and what are they  Jim what are they trying to get and you  point out in the book that we don't seem  prepared for what is happening to us no  question they're trying China's case  they're trying outright to surpass the  US this is not a secret they say it  publicly in speeches it's in their  documents their national security  documents they they want to achieve what  they view as their rightful place on top  of the world and almost invariably  national security folks will say China  is the bigger of the two threats but but  Russia very big threat and and theirs as  more of a zero-sum game any opportunity  to stick their finger in the eye of the  United States they view as a win I spoke  with the FBI director last year and you  think about what the FBI does in turn  of countering terrorist threats he said  his top counterintelligence priority is  China  how many spies Chinese spies are in  America trying to steal and commit  economic espionage thousands here and I  spoke to the FBI's former head of  counterintelligence and tens of  thousands in China I mean he talked  about it in terms of how they have a  national service program almost for  smart young people there to hack their  way into US public and private sector  secrets and they do it with enormous  success they're stealing seed technology  agriculture technology or a fish  intelligence but also crucially national  security technology have a chapter in  the book about how over the course of  four years before they were detected a  small team of four people stole secrets  about the f-35 the c-17 and the f-22 and  today China is flying planes that look  remarkably like those planes so Jim give  us some context in terms of before 9/11  there were people who were saying  connect the darks and there were other  people who were asleep at the switch to  mix my metaphors in this case do people  know the threat is real and they're just  trying to catch up or are they still  blind to the nature of the threat it  took time it was belated but they know  today I spent time out in the field this  is the way u.s. submarine commanders  talk about the conflict today it's the  way people in the NSA operation centers  fighting cyberattacks every day it's the  way they talk about it's the way US  diplomats in Ukraine etc it is not the  way the US president talks about this  threat he will not publicly identify in  fact alarmingly he will often sound very  much like Russia on what's the practical  result of that though because what when  you as you know when you talk to  officials they'll say forget the  rhetoric we're on the case here and the  rhetoric doesn't matter well folks right  and to be clear in this book I spread  the blame around me because through  multiple administration's of Republican  and Democratic parties missed signals  over time everybody thought they could  get it right  the Bush administration thought they  could get it right Obama could get  thought he'd get it right saw the light  later Trump administration not unusual  in that respect unusual though in that  when you see the hostility the president  still won't recognize it and state it  publicly and everybody across the board  says the u.s. cannot  this war defend itself properly without  leadership from the top and they don't  have any leadership well this trade war  with China make this worse well this is  the thing and again credit where credit  is due  the president is confronting China for  instance on the theft of trade secrets  to a degree the previous administrations  would not they knew about it but but  they said listen we could get it right  bring them into the fold they were  change their behavior they have not the  president's confronting the trouble is  what the president is asking China to do  is to change its economic model at state  model this is the way it has achieved  success in its view when you battle like  that and both have advantages will China  back down I'll tell you we have internal  domestic politics so does China the last  thing a Chinese leader is gonna want to  do is be seen as backing down to the US  president help people understand why  presidential leadership is so important  without it what doesn't happen well  things like allocation of resources  making decisions to counter to counter  the threat defending US assets taking  where necessary offensive steps to  counter this threat that requires  presidential leadership it matters that  this president has only had one cabinet  level discussion of election security  that's a problem only one only one it  matters that this president you heard  this from Kirsten Nielsen as she left it  matters that this president that his  senior advisors can't even bring up the  issue of the election and Ference with  him because he won't go there yeah you  made a point of saying you're not  writing this book for politics you're  writing it you said at the end as a  concerned American I was very touched by  that and I am I spent years in Russia  and China and and seeing each front of  this war I've been on the ground in  Ukraine I've been on a u.s. under the  Arctic I've been in the NSA operations  rooms I've been on a u.s. spy plane over  the South China Sea  I see Americans in uniform and out out  of uniform fighting this battle every  day because they care about protecting  their country I care about the safety of  the country I've got three kids I want  them to live in a world as free as I was  able to to grow up in and travel the  world and you have two countries here  that are intent on changing the way the  world operates and if the country and if  our leaders don't fight back it's gonna  be a very different world all right Jim  judo you've written it was really good  you're very good oh my goodness you're a  great  no you're very good yeah really really  good thank you very much  you think you should send a couple  copies over to the White House okay I'll  rub them on yeah I think you should send  an autograph to the shadow war it's  available today wherever you'd like to  buy your books

